# contour_pocket.cam — the 3D-wire pocket rim, slice 1 (DECISIONS.md "the
# 3D-wire Contour…", blessed 2026-07-29). A square rim whose top edge rises
# and falls in Z, swept down by extent=3 — the first feature where both
# halves of `total Z span = the wire's own Z span + extent` are nonzero.
# Both comp modes in one golden (the two-runs pattern).
#
# The wall-only op declares no interior (the stock model reports itself
# incomplete for it, silencing the entry restriction by design) — a real
# part would Clear or Face the region first; this fixture is the standalone
# wall trace.
#
# Hand-checked anchors (60mm square 20..80, T5 dia 10 so r = 5; wire corners
# alternate z = 0 and z = -2, so every side's slope is ±2/60 = ±1/30):
#   - engine comp offsets the projection inward to the sharp square 25..75.
#     Every offset corner is 5mm along BOTH adjacent walls from its wire
#     corner, so its top edge sits 5·(1/30) = 1/6 below/above that corner's
#     own z, and the tie-min rule picks the deeper (equal here by symmetry):
#     corner near (20,20,z=0):  top = -1/6,  cut Z = -1/6  - 3 = -3.167
#     corner near (80,20,z=-2): top = -11/6, cut Z = -11/6 - 3 = -4.833
#   - control comp emits the PART EDGE with a Z word per vertex: the wire's
#     own points at z - 3 (X20 Y20 Z-3.000, X80 Y20 Z-5.000, …), D register
#     the pure tool radius (D5).
units mm
feed 800
plunge 300
rapid_z 5
clearance_z 25
spindle 3000

stock Box(w=100, l=100, h=20, x=0, y=0, z=0)

tool T5 Endmill(dia=10.0)

feature Rim ContourPocket(extent=3.0
    20 20 0
    80 20 -2
    80 80 0
    20 80 -2
)

run Side(tool=T5, surface=Rim)
run Side(tool=T5, surface=Rim, comp=control)
